Package: boswas-branding
Architecture: all
Depends: python3,
         python3-pyside6.qtcore,
         python3-pyside6.qtdbus,
         python3-pyside6.qtgui,
         python3-pyside6.qtnetwork,
         python3-pyside6.qtsvg,
         python3-pyside6.qtwidgets,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: breeze-icon-theme, fonts-inter, fonts-lato
Description: Boswas OS visual identity
 The Boswas OS visual identity, built from the Boswas OS logo (the gold and
 silver "b" mark), the brand typeface and one design system, Boswas UI:
 .
  * the Boswas UI design tokens (the Prism palette) and the Prism colour
    schemes for KDE applications
  * Boswas Prism, the icon pack of the Boswas desktop: applications,
    places, devices, file types and symbolic status and action icons; the
    earlier Boswas and Boswas Light icon themes stay available
  * Orbitron, the brand typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
  * ten Boswas OS presets (Horizon, Midnight, Aurora, Slate, Carbon, Pearl,
    Ocean, Ember, Nebula, Classic): light or dark, wallpapers, lock screen
    art and colour schemes for KDE applications, and boswas-preset to
    switch between them
  * the prompt and welcome of Boswas Terminal (boswas-welcome)
  * boswas_fluent, the Qt (PySide6) toolkit that gives the Boswas
    applications the Boswas UI look: theme, widgets and helpers, from the
    same design tokens
 .
 The desktop that uses them is the package boswas-desktop; the boot screen
 is boswas-bootsplash.
 .
 No KDE program is needed or started. For KDE applications a user
 installs, defaults (the Prism colours, the Boswas Prism icons and the
 Breeze widget style) are delivered through an XDG configuration directory
 (/usr/share/boswas/kde-settings), so /etc/xdg and per-user settings keep
 precedence and no file of another package is modified.
